{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V3H9sTFRtcEzRBYpxYupcx","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"body\":\"> **Scope:** this issue operates on the `luiscipparrone1/locus-landing-page` repository only. All new code lives in `src/app/`, `src/lib/`, `src/middleware.ts`, `emails/`. No changes to the Mac app or the Fastify API.\\n>\\n> **Depends on:** Issue B (billing schema + `entitlements_v` view) must be merged and the migration applied before this issue ships. This issue reads from tables Issue B creates and writes to them via Stripe webhook processing.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nLocus currently has no way to accept money. The landing page is public-only: no authentication, no account area, no billing, no payment flow. To ship the Pro tier the site needs the full stack of paying-customer plumbing — sign up, log in, buy, see what you own, manage it, cancel. The Mac app is getting its entitlement check from the Fastify API (Issue B), but the webhook that populates the `subscriptions` table and the pages users actually interact with live here.\\n\\nBuilding this once, correctly, with idempotent webhooks and minimal moving parts, unblocks everything else.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nAdd Supabase-based authentication (email magic link + Google OAuth + Apple OAuth) via `@supabase/ssr`. Build the three Stripe surfaces a subscription product needs: hosted Checkout (to accept payment), hosted Customer Portal (to manage subscription), and a webhook handler (to sync Stripe state into the database Issue B created). Build `/account` and `/billing` pages that read entitlements + subscription details and render user-facing status. Send three transactional emails via Resend + React Email: welcome, renewal reminder, cancellation. Enforce auth on protected routes with a single `middleware.ts`. Implement the one-shot 7-day \\\"Try Pro\\\" endpoint.\\n\\nEverything Stripe-related lives in `src/lib/stripe/`. Everything Supabase-related lives in `src/lib/supabase/`. Emails live in `src/emails/` with senders in `src/lib/mail/`. No other module knows about Stripe, Supabase, or Resend.\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n1. As a visitor ready to buy, I want to sign up with Google, Apple, or email magic link, so that I don't create yet another password.\\n2. As a signed-up user, I want \\\"Upgrade to Pro\\\" to redirect me to Stripe's hosted checkout, so that I never hand card details to the Locus site.\\n3. As a paying user, I want to return to `/account` after checkout and immediately see \\\"Pro, renews on X\\\", so that I know my purchase succeeded.\\n4. As a paying user, I want \\\"Manage subscription\\\" to open Stripe's Customer Portal in the same tab, so that I can update my card, view invoices, and cancel in one place.\\n5. As a user who just subscribed, I want to receive a welcome email explaining how to sign in on the Mac, so that I can use what I paid for.\\n6. As a yearly subscriber whose renewal is in 7 days, I want a reminder email, so that I can cancel in time if I no longer want it.\\n7. As a user who cancelled, I want a cancellation confirmation email, so that I have a receipt.\\n8. As a signed-in user on `/account`, I want to see my email, plan chip (Free / Trial / Pro), renewal or expiry date, \\\"Manage subscription\\\" button, \\\"Sign out everywhere\\\" button, and a link to `/download`.\\n9. As an unauthenticated visitor clicking `/account`, I want to be redirected to `/login?next=/account`, so that after signing in I land where I intended.\\n10. As a signed-in user clicking `/login`, I want to be redirected to `/account`, so that I don't loop.\\n11. As a Stripe webhook that gets replayed (same event twice), I want the second call to be a no-op, so that retries don't double-grant Pro.\\n12. As a user whose first webhook attempt times out, I want Stripe to retry and the handler to succeed on retry, so that my purchase gets recorded eventually.\\n13. As a user on a flaky network, I want Checkout and Portal failures to show a readable error (not a blank page), so that I can retry.\\n14. As a user who cancelled but is still within the billing period, I want `/account` to show \\\"Pro until <date>, will not renew\\\", so that I know what happens next.\\n15. As a Free user wanting to evaluate Pro, I want to click \\\"Start 7-day Pro trial\\\" (on `/account` or on a future paywall in the Mac app) and immediately get Pro, so that I can try before I buy without entering a card.\\n16. As a user who already consumed their one-shot trial, I want the \\\"Start trial\\\" button to be labeled \\\"Trial already used\\\" and disabled, so that I'm not misled.\\n17. As a developer debugging a webhook, I want every received event visible in the `stripe_events` table with its raw payload, so that I can replay or forensically inspect any event.\\n18. As a user returning after an hour, I want my Supabase session to refresh transparently, so that I don't randomly get logged out mid-browse.\\n19. As a user who clicks \\\"Sign out everywhere\\\", I want every session on every device invalidated, so that a shared or stolen laptop can't keep access.\\n20. As a user who subscribed monthly but wants yearly, I want the Stripe Customer Portal to let me switch plans with proration, so that I don't have to cancel and resubscribe.\\n\\n## Implementation Decisions\\n\\n- **Dependencies added**: `@supabase/ssr`, `@supabase/supabase-js`, `stripe`, `@stripe/stripe-js`, `react-email`, `@react-email/components`, `resend`, `zod`. (PostHog and Vercel Analytics are added separately, scoped under analytics in a follow-up — not blocking this issue.)\\n- **Supabase clients**: `src/lib/supabase/server.ts` exports `createServerClient()` for RSC + route handlers (cookie-based session via Next headers). `src/lib/supabase/browser.ts` exports `createBrowserClient()` for client components. `src/lib/supabase/service.ts` exports a service-role client (used only server-side for admin operations).\\n- **Middleware**: `src/middleware.ts` runs on matchers `['/account/:path*', '/billing/:path*']`. If no Supabase session, 302 redirect to `/login?next=<original>`. No other paths touched; public pages (Issue A) are unaffected.\\n- **Routes added**:\\n  - `/login` — client-rendered form with OAuth buttons + email magic-link input. Posts to Supabase via the browser client. On success, redirects to `next` or `/account`.\\n  - `/signup` — same form; Supabase's magic link flow handles both sign-up and sign-in without distinguishing.\\n  - `/auth/callback` — OAuth return URL. Exchanges the code for a session via `supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession()`, redirects to `next`.\\n  - `/account` — SSR. Reads `entitlements_v` + `subscriptions` + `profiles` + `pro_trials` for the authenticated user via a single query. Renders plan chip, renewal/expiry date, CTA (\\\"Upgrade\\\" / \\\"Manage\\\" / \\\"Start trial\\\"), \\\"Sign out everywhere\\\", link to `/download`.\\n  - `/billing` — thin page containing a \\\"Manage subscription on Stripe\\\" button that POSTs to `/api/billing/portal` and follows the 302.\\n  - `/api/checkout/create` — Node runtime. Authenticated. Body: `{ priceId: 'monthly'|'yearly' }`. Resolves to the corresponding Stripe price ID via env var. Looks up or creates `stripe_customer_id` on the user's `subscriptions` row (stub row created if none exists with `status = 'incomplete'`). Creates a Stripe Checkout Session with `mode: 'subscription'`, `customer: stripe_customer_id`, `line_items: [{ price, quantity: 1 }]`, `success_url: ${origin}/account?welcome=1`, `cancel_url: ${origin}/pricing`. Returns `{ url }`.\\n  - `/api/billing/portal` — Node runtime. Authenticated. Creates a Stripe Customer Portal session. Returns `{ url }`.\\n  - `/api/stripe/webhook` — Node runtime (**must** export `export const runtime = 'nodejs'` — Edge doesn't support raw body / node crypto). Reads raw body via `await request.text()`. Verifies signature via `Stripe.webhooks.constructEvent`. Inserts into `stripe_events` with `ON CONFLICT (stripe_event_id) DO NOTHING`. If insert affected 0 rows (duplicate), returns 200 immediately. Otherwise dispatches to `src/lib/stripe/events/handle.ts`.\\n  - `/api/pro-trial/start` — Node runtime. Authenticated. Executes `INSERT INTO pro_trials (user_id, started_at, expires_at) VALUES ($1, now(), now() + interval '7 days') ON CONFLICT (user_id) DO NOTHING RETURNING expires_at`. Returns `{ started: true, expiresAt }` on insert, `{ started: false, reason: 'already-used' }` on conflict.\\n  - `/api/cron/renewal-reminders` — Vercel Cron (daily). Queries `subscriptions WHERE current_period_end BETWEEN now() + 6 days AND now() + 8 days AND renewal_reminder_sent = false`, sends a reminder email per row, sets `renewal_reminder_sent = true`. Protected by `CRON_SECRET` header check.\\n- **Stripe event handlers** in `src/lib/stripe/events/handle.ts`:\\n  - `checkout.session.completed` → extract `customer`, `subscription`, resolve `user_id` from `client_reference_id` (set at session creation to the Supabase user id), upsert `subscriptions` row with status/period/price from the embedded subscription object. Fire `sendWelcome`.\\n  - `customer.subscription.updated` → locate row by `stripe_subscription_id`, update `status`, `current_period_end`, `cancel_at`, `trial_end`, `price_id`. If status transitions `active → canceled`, fire `sendCancellation`.\\n  - `customer.subscription.deleted` → locate row, set `status = 'canceled'`, `cancel_at = now()`.\\n  - Any other event type → log and return.\\n- **Stripe helpers** in `src/lib/stripe/`:\\n  - `client.ts` — instantiates the Stripe SDK with `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` and `apiVersion: '2024-12-18.acacia'` (pin current).\\n  - `checkout.ts` — `createCheckoutSession(userId, priceId): Promise<{ url: string }>`.\\n  - `portal.ts` — `createPortalSession(userId): Promise<{ url: string }>`.\\n  - `customer.ts` — `getOrCreateCustomer(userId): Promise<string>` (returns Stripe customer ID, creates on Stripe and upserts into `subscriptions` if missing).\\n- **Email provider**: Resend. Templates in `src/emails/` as React Email components: `WelcomeEmail.tsx`, `RenewalReminderEmail.tsx`, `CancellationEmail.tsx`. Senders in `src/lib/mail/`: `sendWelcome(user, { downloadUrl })`, `sendRenewalReminder(user, { renewalDate, plan })`, `sendCancellation(user, { accessUntil })`. Senders render via `@react-email/render` and call `resend.emails.send(...)`. Single `src/lib/mail/client.ts` constructs the Resend client.\\n- **Stripe products** (created in Stripe dashboard, not in code): one Product \\\"Locus Pro\\\", two recurring Prices ($6/mo USD, $58/yr USD). Price IDs stored as `STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY` and `STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY` env vars.\\n- **Stripe Customer Portal configuration** (dashboard): allow cancel immediately, allow cancel at period end, allow payment-method update, allow plan switch monthly ↔ yearly with proration enabled. Do not allow pausing. Do not collect billing address (digital product, no shipping).\\n- **Environment variables** (Vercel project settings, different values per environment):\\n  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`\\n  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\\n  - `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (server-only, never exposed to client)\\n  - `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`\\n  - `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`\\n  - `STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY`\\n  - `STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY`\\n  - `RESEND_API_KEY`\\n  - `CRON_SECRET`\\n  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` (for absolute URLs in emails)\\n- **Supabase OAuth provider setup**: Google and Apple configured in the Supabase dashboard with redirect URL `${NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/auth/callback`. Both dev and prod URLs registered.\\n- **Sign-out everywhere**: `/account` button calls `supabase.auth.signOut({ scope: 'global' })`, which invalidates all refresh tokens for the user. Does not require any custom server endpoint.\\n- **Idempotency model for webhooks**: the `stripe_events` insert-or-skip IS the idempotency guarantee. Processing is never attempted twice for the same `stripe_event_id`. Stripe retries that arrive before the first insert completes are covered by Postgres's row-level lock on the primary key insert.\\n- **Failure handling**: Stripe webhook handler returns 500 on processing error, letting Stripe retry. A processing error after `stripe_events` insert leaves a row with `processed_at` set but no DB side effects — add a background reconciler later if this becomes a real problem; not scoped to this issue.\\n- **Copy**: \\\"Try Pro\\\" on `/account` reads \\\"Free for 7 days, no card needed\\\" when eligible; \\\"Trial used on <date>\\\" when consumed. Hero copy on landing stays \\\"Free forever. Pro when you want it.\\\" (shipped by Issue A).\\n- **No cookie banner in this issue**: no session replay, no GA4. PostHog + consent UI scoped to a later analytics issue.\\n\\n## Testing Decisions\\n\\n- **What makes a good test**: test the *behavior* of the webhook handler and the Checkout/Portal creators with real Stripe event fixtures; do not test the Stripe SDK internals. Test the auth middleware via Playwright because the value is the end-to-end redirect behavior, not unit-level branching.\\n- **Webhook handler tests**: Vitest on `src/lib/stripe/events/handle.ts`. Fixtures are real Stripe event payloads captured via `stripe listen --print-secret > fixture.json` during local development. Test cases:\\n  - `checkout.session.completed` with a valid `client_reference_id` → inserts a `subscriptions` row with correct fields, calls `sendWelcome` (mocked).\\n  - Duplicate event (same `stripe_event_id`) → no-op (returns early from the route, handler not invoked).\\n  - `customer.subscription.updated` transitioning status to `canceled` → updates row, calls `sendCancellation`.\\n  - `customer.subscription.deleted` → marks row canceled.\\n  - Unknown event type → logs, no DB writes, no emails.\\n- **Checkout endpoint tests**: Vitest with mocked Stripe client. Assert (a) customer lookup-or-create is called, (b) Checkout session created with the right price ID from env, (c) success/cancel URLs built from the origin, (d) `client_reference_id` is the Supabase user id.\\n- **Pro-trial endpoint tests**: Vitest against a test DB. Cover (a) fresh user → row inserted with +7-day expiry, (b) user with existing row → `already-used` with no change, (c) concurrent calls → exactly one succeeds (test serializes two parallel requests).\\n- **Middleware Playwright e2e**: single spec that (a) hits `/account` with no session and asserts redirect to `/login?next=%2Faccount`, (b) signs in as a test user via Supabase (using a magic-link intercept or a test-only password user), asserts redirect to `/account`, (c) asserts that subsequent `/account` visits do not redirect.\\n- **Email template tests**: snapshot tests on React Email components. Props vary across snapshots (new user, cancelling user, yearly vs monthly renewal). Snapshots committed. Regenerate on intentional copy changes.\\n- **Not in scope for testing**: the Stripe SDK, the Supabase SDK, real email delivery, real Stripe API calls in CI. Use Stripe test mode locally only.\\n- **Prior art**: `locus-landing-page` has no existing test harness. Introduce Vitest for unit/component tests and Playwright for e2e. Playwright config shared with Issue A's smoke test (Issue A introduces the baseline Playwright setup; this issue adds one additional spec).\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Billing schema and `entitlements_v` view (Issue B).\\n- Mac-app-side handling of the entitlement response (Issue D).\\n- Marketing pages, Pricing copy, FAQ (Issue A).\\n- Team seats, student pricing, regional pricing, coupon codes.\\n- Self-service account deletion with full data export (eventual; not v1).\\n- Two-factor auth, password rotation (Supabase provides this surface; not our code).\\n- Invoicing portal beyond Stripe's default.\\n- In-app purchase or Mac App Store distribution.\\n- PostHog, Vercel Analytics, cookie consent banner (later analytics issue).\\n\\n## Further Notes\\n\\n- Supabase project must be created and provisioned before this issue can merge. Required: anon key, service-role key, OAuth providers configured, production + dev redirect URLs registered.\\n- Stripe account must have test-mode and live-mode products/prices set up, with prices' IDs assigned to the corresponding env vars. Webhook endpoints must be registered in Stripe dashboard pointing at `getlocus.tech/api/stripe/webhook` (live) and the preview/dev equivalent.\\n- Resend domain `getlocus.tech` must have SPF + DKIM records verified.\\n- Emails send from production only (live Stripe mode). Local dev uses Stripe test mode and a Resend test \\\"from\\\" address.\\n- The `client_reference_id` on Stripe Checkout Sessions is the Supabase user id — this is how the webhook handler maps Stripe customers back to our users on first purchase.\\n- Plan switch (monthly ↔ yearly) is handled entirely by Stripe Customer Portal; no custom code needed.\\n\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b359056d-8171-4758-80a4-d865a9a6082e","uuid":"4c251a82-3865-43f1-9680-395079a75e2c","timestamp":"2026-04-26T22:27:39.391Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"body\":\"> **Scope:** this issue operates on the `luiscipparrone1/locus-landing-page` repository only. All new code lives in `src/app/`, `src/lib/`, `src/middleware.ts`, `emails/`. No changes to the Mac app or the Fastify API.\\n>\\n> **Depends on:** Issue B (billing schema + `entitlements_v` view) must be merged and the migration applied before this issue ships. This issue reads from tables Issue B creates and writes to them via Stripe webhook processing.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nLocus currently has no way to accept money. The landing page is public-only: no authentication, no account area, no billing, no payment flow. To ship the Pro tier the site needs the full stack of paying-customer plumbing — sign up, log in, buy, see what you own, manage it, cancel. The Mac app is getting its entitlement check from the Fastify API (Issue B), but the webhook that populates the `subscriptions` table and the pages users actually interact with live here.\\n\\nBuilding this once, correctly, with idempotent webhooks and minimal moving parts, unblocks everything else.\\n\\n## Solution\\n\\nAdd Supabase-based authentication (email magic link + Google OAuth + Apple OAuth) via `@supabase/ssr`. Build the three Stripe surfaces a subscription product needs: hosted Checkout (to accept payment), hosted Customer Portal (to manage subscription), and a webhook handler (to sync Stripe state into the database Issue B created). Build `/account` and `/billing` pages that read entitlements + subscription details and render user-facing status. Send three transactional emails via Resend + React Email: welcome, renewal reminder, cancellation. Enforce auth on protected routes with a single `middleware.ts`. Implement the one-shot 7-day \\\"Try Pro\\\" endpoint.\\n\\nEverything Stripe-related lives in `src/lib/stripe/`. Everything Supabase-related lives in `src/lib/supabase/`. Emails live in `src/emails/` with senders in `src/lib/mail/`. No other module knows about Stripe, Supabase, or Resend.\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n1. As a visitor ready to buy, I want to sign up with Google, Apple, or email magic link, so that I don't create yet another password.\\n2. As a signed-up user, I want \\\"Upgrade to Pro\\\" to redirect me to Stripe's hosted checkout, so that I never hand card details to the Locus site.\\n3. As a paying user, I want to return to `/account` after checkout and immediately see \\\"Pro, renews on X\\\", so that I know my purchase succeeded.\\n4. As a paying user, I want \\\"Manage subscription\\\" to open Stripe's Customer Portal in the same tab, so that I can update my card, view invoices, and cancel in one place.\\n5. As a user who just subscribed, I want to receive a welcome email explaining how to sign in on the Mac, so that I can use what I paid for.\\n6. As a yearly subscriber whose renewal is in 7 days, I want a reminder email, so that I can cancel in time if I no longer want it.\\n7. As a user who cancelled, I want a cancellation confirmation email, so that I have a receipt.\\n8. As a signed-in user on `/account`, I want to see my email, plan chip (Free / Trial / Pro), renewal or expiry date, \\\"Manage subscription\\\" button, \\\"Sign out everywhere\\\" button, and a link to `/download`.\\n9. As an unauthenticated visitor clicking `/account`, I want to be redirected to `/login?next=/account`, so that after signing in I land where I intended.\\n10. As a signed-in user clicking `/login`, I want to be redirected to `/account`, so that I don't loop.\\n11. As a Stripe webhook that gets replayed (same event twice), I want the second call to be a no-op, so that retries don't double-grant Pro.\\n12. As a user whose first webhook attempt times out, I want Stripe to retry and the handler to succeed on retry, so that my purchase gets recorded eventually.\\n13. As a user on a flaky network, I want Checkout and Portal failures to show a readable error (not a blank page), so that I can retry.\\n14. As a user who cancelled but is still within the billing period, I want `/account` to show \\\"Pro until <date>, will not renew\\\", so that I know what happens next.\\n15. As a Free user wanting to evaluate Pro, I want to click \\\"Start 7-day Pro trial\\\" (on `/account` or on a future paywall in the Mac app) and immediately get Pro, so that I can try before I buy without entering a card.\\n16. As a user who already consumed their one-shot trial, I want the \\\"Start trial\\\" button to be labeled \\\"Trial already used\\\" and disabled, so that I'm not misled.\\n17. As a developer debugging a webhook, I want every received event visible in the `stripe_events` table with its raw payload, so that I can replay or forensically inspect any event.\\n18. As a user returning after an hour, I want my Supabase session to refresh transparently, so that I don't randomly get logged out mid-browse.\\n19. As a user who clicks \\\"Sign out everywhere\\\", I want every session on every device invalidated, so that a shared or stolen laptop can't keep access.\\n20. As a user who subscribed monthly but wants yearly, I want the Stripe Customer Portal to let me switch plans with proration, so that I don't have to cancel and resubscribe.\\n\\n## Implementation Decisions\\n\\n- **Dependencies added**: `@supabase/ssr`, `@supabase/supabase-js`, `stripe`, `@stripe/stripe-js`, `react-email`, `@react-email/components`, `resend`, `zod`. (PostHog and Vercel Analytics are added separately, scoped under analytics in a follow-up — not blocking this issue.)\\n- **Supabase clients**: `src/lib/supabase/server.ts` exports `createServerClient()` for RSC + route handlers (cookie-based session via Next headers). `src/lib/supabase/browser.ts` exports `createBrowserClient()` for client components. `src/lib/supabase/service.ts` exports a service-role client (used only server-side for admin operations).\\n- **Middleware**: `src/middleware.ts` runs on matchers `['/account/:path*', '/billing/:path*']`. If no Supabase session, 302 redirect to `/login?next=<original>`. No other paths touched; public pages (Issue A) are unaffected.\\n- **Routes added**:\\n  - `/login` — client-rendered form with OAuth buttons + email magic-link input. Posts to Supabase via the browser client. On success, redirects to `next` or `/account`.\\n  - `/signup` — same form; Supabase's magic link flow handles both sign-up and sign-in without distinguishing.\\n  - `/auth/callback` — OAuth return URL. Exchanges the code for a session via `supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession()`, redirects to `next`.\\n  - `/account` — SSR. Reads `entitlements_v` + `subscriptions` + `profiles` + `pro_trials` for the authenticated user via a single query. Renders plan chip, renewal/expiry date, CTA (\\\"Upgrade\\\" / \\\"Manage\\\" / \\\"Start trial\\\"), \\\"Sign out everywhere\\\", link to `/download`.\\n  - `/billing` — thin page containing a \\\"Manage subscription on Stripe\\\" button that POSTs to `/api/billing/portal` and follows the 302.\\n  - `/api/checkout/create` — Node runtime. Authenticated. Body: `{ priceId: 'monthly'|'yearly' }`. Resolves to the corresponding Stripe price ID via env var. Looks up or creates `stripe_customer_id` on the user's `subscriptions` row (stub row created if none exists with `status = 'incomplete'`). Creates a Stripe Checkout Session with `mode: 'subscription'`, `customer: stripe_customer_id`, `line_items: [{ price, quantity: 1 }]`, `success_url: ${origin}/account?welcome=1`, `cancel_url: ${origin}/pricing`. Returns `{ url }`.\\n  - `/api/billing/portal` — Node runtime. Authenticated. Creates a Stripe Customer Portal session. Returns `{ url }`.\\n  - `/api/stripe/webhook` — Node runtime (**must** export `export const runtime = 'nodejs'` — Edge doesn't support raw body / node crypto). Reads raw body via `await request.text()`. Verifies signature via `Stripe.webhooks.constructEvent`. Inserts into `stripe_events` with `ON CONFLICT (stripe_event_id) DO NOTHING`. If insert affected 0 rows (duplicate), returns 200 immediately. Otherwise dispatches to `src/lib/stripe/events/handle.ts`.\\n  - `/api/pro-trial/start` — Node runtime. Authenticated. Executes `INSERT INTO pro_trials (user_id, started_at, expires_at) VALUES ($1, now(), now() + interval '7 days') ON CONFLICT (user_id) DO NOTHING RETURNING expires_at`. Returns `{ started: true, expiresAt }` on insert, `{ started: false, reason: 'already-used' }` on conflict.\\n  - `/api/cron/renewal-reminders` — Vercel Cron (daily). Queries `subscriptions WHERE current_period_end BETWEEN now() + 6 days AND now() + 8 days AND renewal_reminder_sent = false`, sends a reminder email per row, sets `renewal_reminder_sent = true`. Protected by `CRON_SECRET` header check.\\n- **Stripe event handlers** in `src/lib/stripe/events/handle.ts`:\\n  - `checkout.session.completed` → extract `customer`, `subscription`, resolve `user_id` from `client_reference_id` (set at session creation to the Supabase user id), upsert `subscriptions` row with status/period/price from the embedded subscription object. Fire `sendWelcome`.\\n  - `customer.subscription.updated` → locate row by `stripe_subscription_id`, update `status`, `current_period_end`, `cancel_at`, `trial_end`, `price_id`. If status transitions `active → canceled`, fire `sendCancellation`.\\n  - `customer.subscription.deleted` → locate row, set `status = 'canceled'`, `cancel_at = now()`.\\n  - Any other event type → log and return.\\n- **Stripe helpers** in `src/lib/stripe/`:\\n  - `client.ts` — instantiates the Stripe SDK with `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` and `apiVersion: '2024-12-18.acacia'` (pin current).\\n  - `checkout.ts` — `createCheckoutSession(userId, priceId): Promise<{ url: string }>`.\\n  - `portal.ts` — `createPortalSession(userId): Promise<{ url: string }>`.\\n  - `customer.ts` — `getOrCreateCustomer(userId): Promise<string>` (returns Stripe customer ID, creates on Stripe and upserts into `subscriptions` if missing).\\n- **Email provider**: Resend. Templates in `src/emails/` as React Email components: `WelcomeEmail.tsx`, `RenewalReminderEmail.tsx`, `CancellationEmail.tsx`. Senders in `src/lib/mail/`: `sendWelcome(user, { downloadUrl })`, `sendRenewalReminder(user, { renewalDate, plan })`, `sendCancellation(user, { accessUntil })`. Senders render via `@react-email/render` and call `resend.emails.send(...)`. Single `src/lib/mail/client.ts` constructs the Resend client.\\n- **Stripe products** (created in Stripe dashboard, not in code): one Product \\\"Locus Pro\\\", two recurring Prices ($6/mo USD, $58/yr USD). Price IDs stored as `STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY` and `STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY` env vars.\\n- **Stripe Customer Portal configuration** (dashboard): allow cancel immediately, allow cancel at period end, allow payment-method update, allow plan switch monthly ↔ yearly with proration enabled. Do not allow pausing. Do not collect billing address (digital product, no shipping).\\n- **Environment variables** (Vercel project settings, different values per environment):\\n  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`\\n  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\\n  - `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (server-only, never exposed to client)\\n  - `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`\\n  - `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`\\n  - `STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY`\\n  - `STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY`\\n  - `RESEND_API_KEY`\\n  - `CRON_SECRET`\\n  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` (for absolute URLs in emails)\\n- **Supabase OAuth provider setup**: Google and Apple configured in the Supabase dashboard with redirect URL `${NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/auth/callback`. Both dev and prod URLs registered.\\n- **Sign-out everywhere**: `/account` button calls `supabase.auth.signOut({ scope: 'global' })`, which invalidates all refresh tokens for the user. Does not require any custom server endpoint.\\n- **Idempotency model for webhooks**: the `stripe_events` insert-or-skip IS the idempotency guarantee. Processing is never attempted twice for the same `stripe_event_id`. Stripe retries that arrive before the first insert completes are covered by Postgres's row-level lock on the primary key insert.\\n- **Failure handling**: Stripe webhook handler returns 500 on processing error, letting Stripe retry. A processing error after `stripe_events` insert leaves a row with `processed_at` set but no DB side effects — add a background reconciler later if this becomes a real problem; not scoped to this issue.\\n- **Copy**: \\\"Try Pro\\\" on `/account` reads \\\"Free for 7 days, no card needed\\\" when eligible; \\\"Trial used on <date>\\\" when consumed. Hero copy on landing stays \\\"Free forever. Pro when you want it.\\\" (shipped by Issue A).\\n- **No cookie banner in this issue**: no session replay, no GA4. PostHog + consent UI scoped to a later analytics issue.\\n\\n## Testing Decisions\\n\\n- **What makes a good test**: test the *behavior* of the webhook handler and the Checkout/Portal creators with real Stripe event fixtures; do not test the Stripe SDK internals. Test the auth middleware via Playwright because the value is the end-to-end redirect behavior, not unit-level branching.\\n- **Webhook handler tests**: Vitest on `src/lib/stripe/events/handle.ts`. Fixtures are real Stripe event payloads captured via `stripe listen --print-secret > fixture.json` during local development. Test cases:\\n  - `checkout.session.completed` with a valid `client_reference_id` → inserts a `subscriptions` row with correct fields, calls `sendWelcome` (mocked).\\n  - Duplicate event (same `stripe_event_id`) → no-op (returns early from the route, handler not invoked).\\n  - `customer.subscription.updated` transitioning status to `canceled` → updates row, calls `sendCancellation`.\\n  - `customer.subscription.deleted` → marks row canceled.\\n  - Unknown event type → logs, no DB writes, no emails.\\n- **Checkout endpoint tests**: Vitest with mocked Stripe client. Assert (a) customer lookup-or-create is called, (b) Checkout session created with the right price ID from env, (c) success/cancel URLs built from the origin, (d) `client_reference_id` is the Supabase user id.\\n- **Pro-trial endpoint tests**: Vitest against a test DB. Cover (a) fresh user → row inserted with +7-day expiry, (b) user with existing row → `already-used` with no change, (c) concurrent calls → exactly one succeeds (test serializes two parallel requests).\\n- **Middleware Playwright e2e**: single spec that (a) hits `/account` with no session and asserts redirect to `/login?next=%2Faccount`, (b) signs in as a test user via Supabase (using a magic-link intercept or a test-only password user), asserts redirect to `/account`, (c) asserts that subsequent `/account` visits do not redirect.\\n- **Email template tests**: snapshot tests on React Email components. Props vary across snapshots (new user, cancelling user, yearly vs monthly renewal). Snapshots committed. Regenerate on intentional copy changes.\\n- **Not in scope for testing**: the Stripe SDK, the Supabase SDK, real email delivery, real Stripe API calls in CI. Use Stripe test mode locally only.\\n- **Prior art**: `locus-landing-page` has no existing test harness. Introduce Vitest for unit/component tests and Playwright for e2e. Playwright config shared with Issue A's smoke test (Issue A introduces the baseline Playwright setup; this issue adds one additional spec).\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n\\n- Billing schema and `entitlements_v` view (Issue B).\\n- Mac-app-side handling of the entitlement response (Issue D).\\n- Marketing pages, Pricing copy, FAQ (Issue A).\\n- Team seats, student pricing, regional pricing, coupon codes.\\n- Self-service account deletion with full data export (eventual; not v1).\\n- Two-factor auth, password rotation (Supabase provides this surface; not our code).\\n- Invoicing portal beyond Stripe's default.\\n- In-app purchase or Mac App Store distribution.\\n- PostHog, Vercel Analytics, cookie consent banner (later analytics issue).\\n\\n## Further Notes\\n\\n- Supabase project must be created and provisioned before this issue can merge. Required: anon key, service-role key, OAuth providers configured, production + dev redirect URLs registered.\\n- Stripe account must have test-mode and live-mode products/prices set up, with prices' IDs assigned to the corresponding env vars. Webhook endpoints must be registered in Stripe dashboard pointing at `getlocus.tech/api/stripe/webhook` (live) and the preview/dev equivalent.\\n- Resend domain `getlocus.tech` must have SPF + DKIM records verified.\\n- Emails send from production only (live Stripe mode). Local dev uses Stripe test mode and a Resend test \\\"from\\\" address.\\n- The `client_reference_id` on Stripe Checkout Sessions is the Supabase user id — this is how the webhook handler maps Stripe customers back to our users on first purchase.\\n- Plan switch (monthly ↔ yearly) is handled entirely by Stripe Customer Portal; no custom code needed.\\n\"}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
