     >\n50\t              {view.planLabel}\n51\t            </span>\n52\t            {view.dateLine ? (\n53\t              <span className=\"text-sm text-[var(--fg)]/70\">\n54\t                {view.dateLine}\n55\t              </span>\n56\t            ) : null}\n57\t          </dd>\n58\t        </div>\n59\t      </dl>\n60\t\n61\t      <div className=\"mt-10 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap\">\n62\t        <button\n63\t          type=\"button\"\n64\t          disabled\n65\t          aria-disabled=\"true\"\n66\t          className=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-[var(--accent)] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--accent-foreground)] transition disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-60\"\n67\t        >\n68\t          {view.primaryCta.label}\n69\t        </button>\n70\t\n71\t        {view.trialCta ? (\n72\t          <button\n73\t            type=\"button\"\n74\t            disabled\n75\t            aria-disabled=\"true\"\n76\t            className=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-[var(--fg)]/20 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--fg)] transition disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-60\"\n77\t          >\n78\t            {view.trialCta.label}\n79\t          </button>\n80\t        ) : null}\n81\t\n82\t        <SignOutButton />\n83\t      </div>\n84\t\n85\t      <div className=\"mt-12 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-6\">\n86\t        <Link\n87\t          href=\"/download\"\n88\t          className=\"text-sm text-[var(--accent-text)] underline-offset-4 hover:underline\"\n89\t        >\n90\t          Download Locus for Mac →\n91\t        </Link>\n92\t      </div>\n93\t    </section>\n94\t  )\n95\t}\n96\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports,