{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KHTbDzWtEZXsH1hqvL3bHR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me create my comprehensive report:\n\n## Codebase Analysis Report: Stripe Checkout Tracer Implementation\n\n### 1. Project Structure\n**src/** is organized as:\n- **src/app/** — Next.js App Router (16.2.4) pages/routes\n  - `/auth/callback/` — OAuth callback handler\n  - `/account/` — Protected user account page  \n  - `/login/` — Auth form\n  - `/signup/`, `/pricing/`, `/download/`, `/changelog/`, `/terms/`, `/privacy/` — Marketing pages\n  - `middleware.ts` — **NOT PRESENT** (none found in src/)\n- **src/lib/supabase/** — Database clients:\n  - `browser.ts` — wraps `createBrowserClient()` from `@supabase/ssr`\n  - `server.ts` — wraps `createServerClient()` from `@supabase/ssr` with cookie handling\n  - `service.ts` — service-role client for admin operations (uses `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`)\n- **src/lib/account/** — Account business logic:\n  - `snapshot.ts` — defines types (`Plan`, `Subscription`, `ProTrial`, `Entitlement`) and `loadAccountSnapshot()` function\n  - `derive.ts` — derives UI state from snapshot (`deriveAccountView()`)\n- **src/components/** — UI organized by sections (layout, media, motion, sections, ui)\n- **src/content/** — Static data and tests\n\n### 2. Existing Stripe/Supabase Code\n**NO Stripe code exists.** The package.json does NOT include `stripe` or `@stripe/stripe-js`. Only Supabase dependencies are present:\n- `@supabase/ssr@^0.10.2`\n- `@supabase/supabase-js@^2.104.1`\n\nA `src/lib/stripe/` directory does NOT exist — you'll need to create it.\n\n### 3. Auth Foundation (Issue #15)\nAuth pattern is established and clean:\n- **Browser clients**: `createBrowserClient()` from `/src/lib/supabase/browser.ts` — wraps `@supabase/ssr`'s `createBrowserClient()`\n- **Server clients**: `createServerClient()` from `/src/lib/supabase/server.ts` — wraps SSR's `createServerClient()` with `cookies()` from `next/headers`\n- **Service role**: `createServiceRoleClient()` from `/src/lib/supabase/service.ts` for admin operations\n- **Getting current user**: Pattern is `await supabase.auth.getUser()` (see `/src/app/account/page.tsx` line 17-20)\n- OAuth callback at `/src/app/auth/callback/route.ts` (lines 21-42) exchanges code via `supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code)`\n\n### 4. `/account` Page (Issue #16)\n**File**: `/src/app/account/page.tsx` (95 lines)\n- Loads `AccountSnapshot` via `loadAccountSnapshot(supabase, user.id, user.email)`\n- Derives UI state via `deriveAccountView(snapshot)`\n- **\"Upgrade to Pro\" placeholder** at line 62-69: disabled button with `disabled` + `aria-disabled=\"true\"` attributes\n- **\"Manage subscription\" placeholder** at line 61-62 (for Pro users)\n- Both CTAs are currently **disabled, inert buttons**\n- `SignOutButton` component imported from `./sign-out-button.tsx` (client component with router.push)\n- Button styling uses CSS variables: `bg-[var(--accent)]`, `text-[var(--accent-foreground)]`, etc.\n\nRelated component: `/src/app/account/sign-out-button.tsx` (client component showing the OAuth/session sign-out pattern)\n\n### 5. Testing Setup\n**Vitest configured** (`vitest.config.mts`):\n- Test files co-located: `src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}`\n- Environment: `jsdom`\n- Plugins: `@vitejs/plugin-react`\n- tsconfig paths enabled\n\n**Testing pattern** (from `/src/app/account/page.test.tsx` and `/src/app/auth/callback/route.test.ts`):\n- Uses `vi.mock()` to mock Supabase clients and Next.js modules\n- Example mocks: `@/lib/supabase/server`, `@/lib/account/snapshot`, `next/navigation` (redirect)\n- SSR server components tested by rendering JSX and checking DOM via `@testing-library/react`\n- Async route handlers tested with `NextRequest` + `vi.fn()` to verify side effects\n\n### 6. package.json Dependencies\n**Already installed**:\n- `@supabase/ssr@^0.10.2` ✓\n- `@supabase/supabase-js@^2.104.1` ✓\n- `next@^16.2.4` (BREAKING CHANGES per AGENTS.md — read `/node_modules/next/dist/docs/`)\n- `react@19.2.4`, `react-dom@19.2.4`\n- `zod@^4.3.6` (for schema validation)\n\n**NOT installed**:\n- `stripe@latest` — **will need to add**\n- `@stripe/stripe-js` — **will need to add**\n\n**Dev tools present**: vitest, testing-library, playwright (e2e), eslint, typescript\n\n### 7. Database Schema\n**Tables referenced** (from `/src/lib/account/snapshot.ts` lines 53-73):\n- `entitlements_v` — view returning `{ user_id, plan }`\n- `subscriptions` — table with `{ user_id, status, current_period_end, cancel_at, price_id }`\n- `profiles` — table with `{ user_id, email }`\n- `pro_trials` — table with `{ user_id, started_at, expires_at }`\n\nTypes defined in `snapshot.ts`:\n```typescript\ntype Plan = \"free\" | \"trial\" | \"pro\"\ntype SubscriptionStatus = \"active\" | \"canceled\" | \"incomplete\" | \"incomplete_expired\" | \"past_due\" | \"trialing\" | \"unpaid\" | \"paused\"\ntype Subscription = { user_id, status, current_period_end, cancel_at, price_id }\n```\n\n**NOTE**: No `customers` or `checkout_sessions` table visible yet — you'll need to design/create schema for Stripe integration.\n\n### 8. Environment Variables\n**Direct access pattern** (no typed wrapper currently):\n- `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` (public, lines referenced in multiple files)\n- `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (public)\n- `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` (public, used in `/src/app/login/login-form.tsx` line 21)\n- `process.env.SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (private, server-only, line in `/src/lib/supabase/service.ts` line 8)\n\n**No typed env wrapper found.** You may want to add one (e.g., using `zod` to validate/type env vars at startup).\n\n---\n\n## Key Conventions to Follow\n\n1. **Auth pattern**: Always use `createServerClient()` in server components/route handlers, `createBrowserClient()` in client components. Never expose service role key to browser.\n2. **Testing**: Mock Supabase via `vi.mock(\"@/lib/supabase/server\")` etc.; test async server components by rendering and checking for thrown redirects.\n3. **Database queries**: Use `supabase.from(table).select(...).maybeSingle()` pattern seen in `snapshot.ts`.\n4. **Type safety**: Types for DB objects should live in `src/lib/account/` (or new `src/lib/stripe/` module).\n5. **UI patterns**: Buttons use CSS variables (`--accent`, `--fg`, etc.); disabled states use `disabled` + `aria-disabled=\"true\"` + class-based opacity.\n6. **No middleware.ts in the root** — auth redirects are done via `redirect()` from `next/navigation` inside server components."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b359056d-8171-4758-80a4-d865a9a6082e","uuid":"c33e8686-986e-4cb1-b741-89e21818e609","timestamp":"2026-04-26T22:29:16.586Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I'm working on a Locus landing page Next.js project at /Users/cippa/Desktop/fly/locus-landing-page-preview. I need to implement a Stripe Checkout tracer (issue #17). I need to understand the current state of the codebase so I can add Stripe integration without breaking conventions.\n\nPlease report back on (be concise, under 400 words):\n\n1. **Project structure**: Show the layout of `src/` — particularly `src/lib/`, `src/app/`, `src/middleware.ts` if it exists.\n2. **Existing Stripe/Supabase code**: Is there ANY existing Stripe code? Any `src/lib/stripe/` directory? Existing Supabase clients in `src/lib/supabase/`?\n3. **Auth foundation** (issue #15 was closed): How is auth set up? Where are `createServerClient`, `createBrowserClient` exported from? How does a route handler get the current user (look for patterns like `supabase.auth.getUser()`)?\n4. **`/account` page** (issue #16 was closed): Show the structure of `src/app/account/page.tsx` and any related components. What does the \"Upgrade to Pro\" placeholder look like currently? Is there a buttons.tsx or client component file?\n5. **Existing tests**: Is Vitest confi